  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 222 PM EDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nAnother pleasant afternoon on the fringe of Northeast US high \npressure. Stratus as seeped into our area from earlier convection \nelsewhere in the Midwest which he limited temperatures toward \nMonticello and Logansport. Highs well into the 80s on Sunday (cloud \ndebris permitting) as upper-level heights rise as a strong ridge to \nour west noses in.\n\nStatus quo once more for severe weather concerns Sunday night and \nMonday. 12z CAM runs remain split on any convection Sunday night, \nwith the HRRR and Fv3 perhaps appearing as outliers with robust \nconvection within our forecast area. Forecast soundings continue to \ndepict an environment ripe for convection awaiting an ample trigger. \nCAPE will be plentiful, even during the overnight hours at greater \nthan 1,500 j/kg, 0-6km shear in excess of 40 knots, and mid-level \nlapse rates near 8C/km. The possibility of decaying convection over \nfar northeast Iowa Sunday morning will need to be monitored as any \noutflow or lingering MCV could serve as a forcing mechanism for our \nlocal area Sunday night. As mentioned in the preceding AFD, the \nthunderstorm risk is confined to the overnight hours consisting \nprimarily of damaging wind gusts. Confidence in severe storms \noccurring Sunday night is still low given a general absence of \nconvection in most CAMs, but cannot completely wave the \"all clear\" \nflag given the anticipated mesoscale nuances to come Sunday. \n\nSimilarly, no significant changes in thinking to Monday night, but \nperhaps a better concensus that this round is the one to watch for \nour area now that the Four Corners ridge is farther east. Again, the \ndevil is in the mesoscale details that remain to be seen. High \npressure descends from central Canada later Tuesday and through \nWednesday offering a break from hot and stormy conditions. The \nwestern US ridge remains in place, but troughing over the Great \nLakes keeps temperatures seasonable with intermittent chances for \nshowers and thunderstorms.",
